    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always seen math as a tool, not a subject I'm naturally good at. It’s logical and precise, which I appreciate. I enjoy it when it connects to real-world problems, like in economics or even in painting, where proportions matter. I'm not confident in my problem-solving speed, which is frustrating sometimes, but I work on it. It's not something I feel passionate about, but it's useful.",
